digraph decision_tree {
  rankdir=TB;
  bgcolor="#0d0e12";
  node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10, fillcolor="#181a20", color="#343846", fontcolor="#e2e8f0"];
  edge [color="#3b82f6", fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9, fontcolor="#93c5fd"];

  history [
    label="1. Prior-journal learning pass (python3 scripts/stats.py at 2026-10-31T09:02Z)\nSettled: 2 WIN, 5 LOSS, 3 EXPIRED with pct, 2 EXPIRED never filled. Sum +4.23%, win rate 28.6%,\navg win +1.51%, avg loss -1.12%. n=12 terminal, mixed setups: no directional inference taken from aggregates.\nLessons checked against each folder's own review.md / trade.toml / decision_tree.dot and used here:\n- LOSS-1.50%_2026-10-23T1147Z_ZECUSDT (LONG limit 1203, SL 1185) filled 22:30Z and stopped 22:35Z, inside the\n  same 5-minute candle, because the stop sat inside the structure being tested.\n- LOSS-1.30%_2026-10-19T1533Z_XRPUSDT (SHORT limit 1.3065, SL 1.3235) was stopped by the squeeze it was fading\n  because the stop sat inside the squeeze reach.\n  -> Applied today: the first draft used SL 611.50, just above the single 435.6 XMR wall at 610.00. Jev put\n  P(that stop is beyond a measured extreme rather than inside the 604-615 block) at 0.13, so the stop was moved to\n  615.50, above the whole 1,233 XMR block (Jev: structurally sound 0.79). EV was given up for that: +0.9310% ->\n  +0.80705% per order.\n- EXPIRED_2026-10-18T1730Z_AVAXUSDT and EXPIRED_2026-10-28T0840Z_ZECUSDT (never touched): fill probability must be\n  carried separately and an unfilled order pays 0 -> P(fill) 0.70 is priced explicitly, EV/order = 0.70 x EV/fill.\n- EXPIRED+1.14%_ZECUSDT, EXPIRED+1.73%_UNIUSDT, EXPIRED+3.95%_ASTERUSDT: non-TP exits are often partial gains, so\n  the expiry branch is real; here it was conservatively carried at 0 while P(inside 588-604 at expiry) = 0.63.\n- EXPIRED+3.95%_2026-10-18T1535Z_ASTERUSDT: TP placed at a range extreme (0.721) was never filled while price\n  peaked 0.7190 -> today the TP 589.00 sits at the top of the measured 588.20-590.20 bid shelf, not at the 574.08 low.\n- WIN+1.26%_2026-10-27T0919Z_ASTERUSDT: selling measured supply with a stop beyond the regime extreme is the one\n  setup shape that has worked here; today's ticket is built the same way, only with the stop beyond the whole block.\n- LOSS-0.72%_2026-10-29T1149Z_BTCUSDT: a measured ask-wall fade still lost when the wall was consumed; that is why\n  today's fill probability (0.70) and the SL-first branch (0.21) are priced rather than assumed away.\nProcess note: PENDING_2026-10-25T1228Z_CAKEUSDT and PENDING_2026-10-30T0845Z_BNBUSDT are OPEN, not settled, and were\nNOT used as evidence.\n"
    fillcolor="#1e293b" color="#3b82f6"
  ];

  extract [
    label="2. Chart extraction (image 261031_10h00m21s_screenshot.png, XMRUSDT 1h, Aster)\nFooter clock 20:44:57 UTC+1; header O590.75(?) H596.70 L588.60 C596.70 +6.30 (+1.07%); last printed 596.70.\nPixel method: candles isolated by exact theme colours (green 30/124/87, red 173/69/70) in a 1080x1920 RGB array;\nprice axis calibrated on detected gridline rows (y=77 -> 668.00, 33 px per 4.00 units, 29 labels 672.00..556.00,\nresidual 0.03 at the 596.70 dotted rule); time axis calibrated on detected day gridlines x=227 (23 Oct) ..\n1811 (31 Oct), 197-198 px/day, 8.22 px/hour, plus a 10-bar right margin; bar grid anchored on body centres\n(x=1778 = last bar) and stepped back 8.223 px per hour.\nResult: 208 hourly bars 2026-10-22T04:00Z .. 2026-10-30T19:00Z. Validation against venue klines: four sampled bars\nmatch Aster perp within +/-0.30 (0.05%), and the two levels TradingView itself highlighted on the axis (564.00 /\n660.66) reproduce as 564.24 / 660.73. Extraction limits: wick extremes good to about +/-0.35.\nStaleness: capture 2026-10-30T19:44Z vs evaluation 09:01Z = 13.3h, so the last 14 bars were replaced/appended with\nlive Aster perp klines (2026-10-30T20:00Z..2026-10-31T09:00Z) and the whole read was re-anchored at 09:21Z.\nMeasured structure: 8-day range 564.24 (24 Oct 00:00Z) - 660.73 (22 Oct 06:00Z); 29 Oct 20:00Z spike\nO601.48 H651.13 L598.29 C624.19 then failed highs 643.13 and 642.13; 30 Oct 14:00Z flush O588.00 H604.13 L574.08\nC599.40; last 18 bars compress 588.23-604.38 with rising lows (588.2, 588.6, 589.8, 590.0, 590.1, 593.0, 594.8,\n595.5) and falling highs (604.2, 602.1, 602.1, 600.0, 600.6, 601.8, 598.7, 596.4); ATR(12) 5.53 = 0.93% vs\nATR(48) 10.29 = 1.73%; 24h high 604.79-604.81 / low 574.08-574.40 across Aster, Binance, Bybit.\n"
    fillcolor="#0f2a43" color="#38bdf8"
  ];

  scen [
    label="3. Scenarios and level probabilities - jev_noul, all on the 2026-10-31T09:15Z state (exact propositions recorded)\nScenario set (closed by a completeness probe):\n  A range-hold, hourly closes 588-604          (Jev: closes stay inside 586-606 = 0.51; inside 588-604 at 05:00Z = 0.63)\n  B break down through 588 toward 574          (sustained break below 588 more likely than above 604 = 0.48)\n  C break up through 604 toward 610-615        (P(604 before 588) = 0.49; P(touch 610 at all in 24h) = 0.26)\n  D news-driven whipsaw through both edges     (P(resumption headline before 05:00Z) = 0.26; P(>1% fall within 2h) = 0.45)\n  Probe: 'a materially different scenario beyond A-D is needed' = 0.22 -> set closed, no new candidates needed.\nLevel / ordering propositions (separate overlapping yes/no - never summed or normalised here):\n  flush 574.08 was a stop-run not the first leg of a breakdown 0.71 | 588.20-590.20 is real demand 0.62 |\n  651 spike + lower highs = distribution 0.75 | P(touch 588.00 in 24h) 0.60 | P(touch 604.00) 0.64 |\n  P(touch 584.00) 0.45 | P(touch 610.00) 0.26 | P(touch 574.08) 0.36 | 24h high > 604.38 0.47 |\n  24h low < 574.08 0.36 | compression resolves up 0.51 | 574.08 still the 48h low at 01 Nov 09:00Z 0.70 |\n  'buy 588-590 dips better supported than sell 600-604 rallies' 0.57 | volatility stays compressed 0.62 |\n  604-615 block absorbs any rally below 610 0.67 | sweep above 610 then reject > acceptance 0.78.\nReading: a two-sided compression with a mild fade-of-supply tilt. The forecast does not need a dominant scenario;\nthe ticket is a fade of measured supply, not a directional bet on B or C.\n"
    fillcolor="#1e1b4b" color="#8b5cf6"
  ];

  research [
    label="4. Research (Jev-defined agenda; full dated log with links in research_log.txt)\nAgenda jev_decide (2026-10-31T09:18Z): positioning_structure 0.75 > market_wide_calendar 0.10 > no_research 0.08 >\nevent_and_catalyst 0.06, confidence 0.71. One agent pass, snapshots 09:07-09:17Z, plus a re-anchor at 09:21:47Z.\nFindings that changed the forecast and the ticket:\n- 29 Oct 20:24Z: 167,464 ETH (~$388M) left 'Binance 14'; Binance paused withdrawals, called it a security incident;\n  $2B-5.7B reported, Tether/Circle froze >$2.3B. XMR got a privacy-coin haven bid (+~6% to ~$637) inside that hour.\n  That bid was LEVERAGED: Binance OI +4.9% and Bybit +15.9% inside the 20:00Z hour. Since then Binance OI -7.0%/24h,\n  -9.3%/72h (below the pre-spike level) while Gate OI +22%/24h, +89%/72h: leverage redistributed, not gone.\n- The 574.08 flush did NOT force-unwind: Binance OI -582 XMR in that hour, Bybit OI rose through it.\n- Funding never negative on any venue in 48h; peaks 0.05-0.086%/8h, now 0.010-0.029%/8h; next print 16:00Z (in window).\n- Crowd is long (Binance accounts L/S 1.7663 = 63.9% long and rising), taker buy share 48.5% over 24h, and the last two\n  completed hours were strongly sell-side (buy/sell 0.685, 0.673). Kraken spot book ask-heavy 0.4:1.\n- Book geometry: to 604.00 costs ~1,176 XMR of asks (~$700k); to 588.00 costs ~2,947 XMR of bids (~$1.75M), 2.5x more.\n  Walls: bid 593.80 x 498.5, 590.36 x 318.7, 590.40 x 248.2, 587.43 x 247.8; ask 610.00 x 435.6, 604-615 = 1,233 XMR.\n- Withdrawal resumption guided to Sunday 1 Nov (co-founder: 'within 42 hours' of 31 Oct 06:00Z) -> at or just beyond the\n  19.5h window, but the headline risk sits inside it and it is what would retire the haven bid.\nNot found: liquidation totals / long-short split / liquidation clusters (Binance forceOrders 401, Bybit endpoints 404,\nCoinglass needs a key, Gate's counter is empty); exchange netflow for XMR; KuCoin/MEXC funding history; Aster OI history.\nNo liquidation claim is used anywhere in this trade.\nPost-research Jev shifts: P(rally into 600-604 is sold rather than breaking 610) 0.86 | P(haven-bid decay is a downside\ndriver over 24h) 0.81 | P(588-592 shelf is consumed rather than refreshed if tested) 0.40 (so the shelf likely holds) |\nP(up-resolution more likely than down once research is included) 0.59 - the two readings pull in opposite directions and\nare both carried.\n"
    fillcolor="#14261c" color="#22c55e"
  ];

  candS [
    label="5. CAND S (selected): SHORT LIMIT 601.50 / TP 589.00 / SL 615.50 / expire 2026-11-01T05:00Z\nEntry 601.50 = lower half of the 600-604 ask band that capped the last 18 bars (604.2 / 602.1 / 602.1 / 600.0 /\n  600.6 / 601.8) and inside the 740+436 XMR ask stack; Jev P(fill before 05:00Z) 0.70, and 'reachable enough to\n  place' 0.90; preferred over 604.00 (fill 0.52) and 602.50 (fill 0.63) on order-level EV.\nTP 589.00 = top of the measured 588.20-590.20 bid shelf (1,291 XMR in 588-592, ~343 in 588-590) and above the\n  584.0-584.8 secondary shelf, not at the 574.08 extreme (EXPIRED+3.95% ASTER lesson).\nSL 615.50 = above the whole 604-615 supply block and its 610.00 wall; Jev 'structurally sound invalidation' 0.79 and\n  P(touch 615.50 before 05:00Z) only 0.11.\nG +2.07811% | L -2.32751% | RR 0.8929 | p_BE 0.52835 | p_TP 0.79 | EV/fill +1.15293% | EV/order +0.80705%\nSensitivity EV/order: 0.75/0.65 -> +0.69547%; 0.70/0.60 -> +0.45385%; 0.65/0.55 -> +0.24359%. Positive in every case.\n"
    fillcolor="#272015" color="#eab308"
  ];

  candL [
    label="6. Candidates evaluated independently and rejected (real levels, same expiry)\nLONG LIMIT 589.00 / TP 602.00 / SL 583.00: p_fill 0.66, p_TP 0.63, p_BE 0.3158 -> EV/order +0.6690%.\n  Rejected: lower EV/order than the short, it buys into the crowded long side (63.9% of accounts) against the\n  haven-bid decay, its stop at 583 sits inside the 580-588 bid shelf (the exact LOSS-1.50% ZEC mistake), and its\n  conditional path (602 before 583 = 0.63) is weaker than the short's (589 before 615.50 = 0.79).\nLONG LIMIT 589.00 / TP 602.00 / SL 579.00: p_TP 0.68, p_BE 0.4348 -> EV/order +0.6320%. Rejected: same, and the\n  wider stop buys only 0.05 of p_TP for 0.68pp of risk.\nLONG LIMIT 585.50 / TP 599.00 / SL 578.00: p_fill 0.33, p_TP 0.57, p_BE 0.3571 -> EV/order +0.2519%. Rejected: fill is\n  a 1.6% breakdown ask and Jev P(touch 584 at all in 24h) is only 0.45.\nSHORT LIMIT 604.00 / TP 589.50 / SL 615.50: p_fill 0.52, p_TP 0.70, p_BE 0.4423 -> EV/order +0.5768%. Rejected: better\n  price, materially worse fill probability, lower EV/order.\nSHORT LIMIT 601.50 / TP 589.00 / SL 611.50: EV/order +0.9310% - the highest raw number, but the stop sits inside the\n  604-615 block (Jev 0.13 that it is beyond a measured extreme). Rejected on structure, not on EV; the trade-off is\n  recorded rather than hidden.\nSHORT MARKET ~596.20 / TP 589.00 / SL 615.50: p_BE 0.680 vs a conditional p_TP well below it -> negative/unsupported;\n  also 'fill probability stated separately' is contradicted for a market order. Rejected.\nNO_TRADE: Jev battery share 0.02; the ticket is positive under every tested assumption, so abstaining would be a\n  preference, not an evidence conclusion.\n"
    fillcolor="#2a1818" color="#ef4444"
  ];

  forecast [
    label="7. Independent forecast (chart_prediction.svg; graphpoints.csv rows 2026-10-31T10:00Z..2026-11-01T05:00Z)\nModal path, contested: chop 594-596 through the morning -> gradual grind up the falling-highs line 596.4 -> 598.8 ->\n  600.9 by 17:00Z -> 601.6 at 18:00Z (the 601.50 limit fills into the 600-604 ask band) -> rejection -> fade 600.4 ->\n  597.8 -> 595.0 -> 593.6 overnight -> 592.2 -> 591.0 -> 590.0 -> 589.0 at 04:00Z (TP zone tagged) -> 590.8 at expiry.\nWhy this shape: 18-bar compression with rising lows and falling highs (A 0.51 / closes in the box 0.63), thin asks to\n  604 (2.5x cheaper to reach than 588) but 0.86 that a rally into 600-604 is sold, and 0.79 that 589 comes before\n  615.50 after a fill. The path needs neither a break of 604 nor a break of 588.\nContested markers carried explicitly: B (a break below 588 toward 574, taps 0.36) would stop the ticket out at expiry or\n  take the trade to a good expiry gain without the TP; C (a break above 604 toward 610-615, P(610) 0.26) fills the\n  entry then runs to the 615.50 stop; D (resumption headline, 0.26 inside the window) can reprice the whole map in one\n  hour in either direction. The forecast was drawn from the modal path and was not bent to the levels; it happens to\n  touch entry then TP.\n"
    fillcolor="#2a2338" color="#c084fc"
  ];

  checks [
    label="8. Contradictions, robustness and validation\n- Ordering violation recorded: P(589 before 611.00 | fill 601.50) = 0.80 but P(589 before 615.50 | fill 601.50) = 0.79,\n  although a wider stop cannot lower the TP-first probability. The lower figure is used in the arithmetic; the\n  difference does not change the sign or the rank of any candidate.\n- Requirement conflict resolved by structure, not by counting: the final Jev battery marked the short ticket's third\n  requirement ('stop beyond a measured structural extreme') supported, while a direct noul put P(611.50 being beyond\n  the block) at 0.13. The stop was moved to 615.50 and the EV cost (+0.9310% -> +0.80705% per order) was accepted.\n- Wide-stop trap tested: EV is not manufactured by widening. At 615.50 the ticket needs p_TP > 0.5284 to be positive\n  and Jev's lowest tested value is 0.65 (EV/order +0.24359%).\n- Two-sided evidence kept: book geometry favours an up move (604 is 2.5x cheaper to reach than 588) while positioning\n  and flow favour a down move (crowded longs, 48.5% taker buy share, ask-heavy spot book, decaying haven bid). The\n  ticket is a fade at a measured level, so it does not need the book-dominance question settled.\n- Freshness: chart capture 2026-10-30T19:44Z was 13.3h stale; 14 live bars were appended and the read was re-anchored\n  at 09:21:47Z (Aster 596.14, Binance 596.53, Bybit 596.55). Jev: 'premise still valid at 596.2 without moving any\n  level' 0.87; 'the 0.11% drift requires moving levels' 0.05. No level touched since (high 596.33, low 594.81).\n- Scenario completeness probe run; 0.22 -> set closed.\n- Model limits stated: no fees, funding, slippage or partial fills in this journal; the SL fills at its level on touch,\n  so the worst case is exactly -2.32751% and no more.\n- Heatmap/liquidation data unavailable (see research), so no cluster levels were used anywhere; order-book levels were\n  used only as zone confirmation for entry/TP/SL placement, never as triggers.\n"
    fillcolor="#2d1b24" color="#f43f5e"
  ];

  terminal [
    label="FINAL: GO LIMIT (PENDING)\nXMRUSDT SHORT LIMIT 601.50 | TP 589.00 (+2.07811%) | SL 615.50 (-2.32751%) | RR 0.89\nP(fill 19.5h) 0.70 | P(TP before SL | fill) 0.79 | p_BE 0.52835 | EV/fill +1.15293% | EV/order +0.80705%\nPlace 2026-10-31T09:40Z | Expire 2026-11-01T05:00Z\n"
    shape=ellipse fillcolor="#1e293b" color="#eab308" fontcolor="#fef08a"
  ];

  history -> extract; extract -> scen; scen -> research; research -> candS; research -> candL;
  candS -> forecast; candL -> forecast [style=dashed color="#ef4444" label="rejected"];
  candS -> checks; candL -> checks [style=dashed color="#ef4444"];
  forecast -> checks; checks -> terminal;
}